{"name":"Oxford Blue","hex":"#002147","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oxford","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Oxford (cloth)","Alternative letter-case form of Oxford (shoe)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxford"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oxford Blue (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Oxford Blue, a shade of navy blue, is the official colour of the University of Oxford. The official Oxford branding guidelines set its definition as Pantone 282, equivalent to the hex code #002147."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Oxford_Blue_colour_square.svg/330px-Oxford_Blue_colour_square.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford_Blue_(colour)","wikidata":"Q7115244"},{"title":"Oxford Blue (cheese)","blocks":[{"text":"Oxford Blue is a variety and brand of blue cheese produced in Burford, Oxfordshire, England in 1995 by French baron Robert Pouget in the tradition of Stilton cheese but with a creamier consistency especially when the cheese was allowed to mature. It is a soft and creamy cheese that has tangy, aromatic and spicy qualities. By 2013, around five tonnes were produced monthly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Oxford_Blue_cheese_1.jpg/330px-Oxford_Blue_cheese_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford_Blue_(cheese)","wikidata":"Q26813710"},{"title":"Blue (university sport)","blocks":[{"text":"A blue is an award of sporting colours earned by athletes at some universities and schools for competition at the highest level. The awarding of blues began at Oxford and Cambridge universities in England. They are now awarded at a number of other British universities and at some universities in Australia and New Zealand."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_(university_sport)","wikidata":"Q4928811"},{"title":"Oxford","blocks":[{"text":"Oxford is a cathedral city and non-metropolitan district in Oxfordshire, England, of which it is the county town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Museum_of_Oxford_%285652685943%29.jpg/330px-Museum_of_Oxford_%285652685943%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford","wikidata":"Q34217"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg/500px-Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg/500px-Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cambridge University Rifle Association half blue blazer and bow tie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg/330px-Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg/330px-Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oxford University Rifle Club half blue blazer and tie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/